  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Response Map: World Vision Digital Accountability for Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Response Map is an online feedback platform which facilitates online tracking, compilation and visual mapping of communications received by targeted communities in Zimbabwe. This tool has been developed by IOM to improve community engagement and two-way communications.  World Vision International (WVI) is implementing activities but lacks a system for recording and following up on community feedback and complaints. To respond to this challenge, IOM will develop a customized instance of Community Response Map for the WVI context. The interactive dashboard enables project managers and decisionmakers to assess the effectiveness of interventions across various metrics including geography, gender, age, and level of comprehension over time. The integration of a coordinated and systematic feedback component in WVI programming will allow the project to measure the impact, geographical reach and gaps in coverage of activities to targeted communities.</narrative>
  </description>
